@nsobid-7E1DF8E08D60544BBDCA1E333C153C97

# Xenoblade Chronicles: Definitive Edition 2.0.0 - 60 FPS

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Unlocks the frame rate to 60 FPS.
//
// The game never sets an NVN present interval; it paces itself with a CPU
// wait at the end of each frame that spins until the elapsed time reaches
// (1/60 s) x swap interval x 0.997. The swap interval is a global int written
// by a single setter, called once at boot with 2 (30 FPS). The same global
// scales the dynamic resolution load metric's frame budget, so requesting 1
// moves both the frame limiter and the resolution scaler to a 16.7 ms budget.
//
// The layer (UI) manager advances its animations by a fixed per-frame step
// that its constructor seeds from a {30.0, 1/30} rodata pair; nothing else
// writes that step. At 60 FPS it would run menus and HUD animations at double
// speed, so the 1/30 half of the pair becomes 1/60. The adjacent rodata loads
// are 8-byte reads of other constants and do not overlap this word.
//
// Gameplay, cutscenes and effects take their step from the update context,
// but a few waits still count updates in 30 Hz frames and would halve at 60
// FPS. Each starts at twice its stock count: the player camera's 5-update
// input lock after a reset, a menu's 30-update input hold after a voice line,
// a menu's 8-update delay before its sound or voice call, the 5-update delay
// before a menu hint animation starts, and the 10- and 60-update holds at
// black between fades in a field sequence.
//
// Menu layout animations are baked with one key per animation frame, and the
// layer applies the key at the whole frame with no blending, so menus and
// pop-ups animate at 30 Hz even at 60 FPS. The two keyframe samplers now blend
// the current key with the next one by the fractional frame when the next key
// is exactly one frame later, which leaves holds and jumps as authored. The
// position, matrix and colour channels take both key values and blend them,
// and the pattern channel keeps the current key. The setup code fits in the
// samplers' parent combine blocks, which are rewritten more compactly.

@enabled
005F02B0 20008052   // MOVZ W0,#1 = swap interval 1 (was ORR W0,WZR,#2 at boot)
009D0ADC 8988883C   // 1/60f layer manager frame step (was 1/30f, 0x3D088889)
// Update-counted waits start at twice the stock count
000529B0 0824A852   // MOV W8, #0x41200000 = camera input lock 10.0 after a reset (was 5.0)
00052B94 0824A852   // MOV W8, #0x41200000 = camera input lock 10.0 after a reset (was 5.0)
001E8748 48018052   // MOV W8, #10 = menu hint animation delay (was 5)
002D5214 88078052   // MOV W8, #60 = menu input hold after a voice line (was 30)
0031F4EC 08028052   // MOV W8, #16 = menu sound or voice call delay (was 8)
0055598C 88028052   // MOV W8, #20 = field sequence hold at black (was 10)
00556A38 080F8052   // MOV W8, #120 = field sequence hold at black (was 60)
